<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Inishowen</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Inishowen is the largest peninsula in Ireland, in the north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-donegal">County Donegal</a> between Lough Swilly and Lough Foyle, ending at Malin Head, the most northerly point of the island. Its name means 'Eógan's island', after the ancestor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cenel-neogain">Cenél nEógain</a>, whose royal fort of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grianan-of-aileach">Grianan of Aileach</a> stands near its southern edge.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/inishowen.jpg" alt="Inishowen" width="320" height="408" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Angr · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Inishowen.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
